    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d441">

                <pb facs="0374" n="368" xml:id="pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163P92/249: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dooman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-08-11T13:00:00+09:00">August 11, 1939—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 11—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>399. Department’s 248, August 9, 8 p.m.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d441-f1"/> On July
                    13 I addressed to the Minister for Foreign Affairs a formal note emphatically
                    objecting to continued occupation of Palmetto Presbyterian Mission property at
                    Soochow and asking that arrangement be made for compensation for losses. A copy
                    of the note was forwarded to the Department with my despatch No. 4036, July
                        14.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d441-f2"/> I asked the Foreign Office today to
                    expedite reply.</p>
                <p>Shanghai please repeat to Chungking and Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dooman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
